    "top_frame": "Logan Webb collapsed and the bats never caught up, leaving Pittsburgh with the last word.",
    "what_this_means": "Blowout losses carve up confidence faster than close ones. Webb lasted two innings, surrendering nine hits and nine runs. The bullpen held what remained. Perdomo was clean for four. But early damage doesn't get undone by competent relief. Turner Hill went 4-for-5 with an RBI and Cavanaugh contributed two more, but sixteen hits for twelve runs tells the real story: runners moved and scoring dried up. Furman tied it in the eighth; Pittsburgh answered in the ninth. This is what inconsistency looks like when it matters. The lineup has shown it can hit. It hasn't shown it can do it consistently enough to survive a starter leaving after two innings.",
